WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.750
Hey, David, why do most white people vote
for Republicans?

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:11.639
This is this is a complex question that requires
a lot of different exploration.

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:16.340
And the answer is not because white people
are more.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.470
Racist and they vote for Republicans that
that's not if that's what you believe, it's

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.060
overly simplistic.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.500
There are, of course, elements of racism,
but that's really not what this is about.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.880
So it is true that when you look at current
polling and you slice and dice it demographically

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.030
by age, by race, by income, you know, all
these different things, by education.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:38.850
Donald Trump is winning among men by not not
by a huge margin.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.350
Donald Trump is winning among white voters.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:45.270
And Donald Trump is winning among uneducated
voters.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:49.030
The more education you have, the more likely
you are to support Joe Biden.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:55.949
The answer to a lot of the white support for
Republicans actually is religion.

00:00:55.949 --> 00:01:02.100
And I want people to be very, very carefully
understanding what it is that I'm saying here.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:07.190
White evangelicals overwhelmingly vote for
Republicans.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:13.100
White non evangelicals are pretty split between
the Democratic and the Republican Party.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.880
So to say it another way.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.310
Were it not for white evangelicals?

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:24.280
The Republican Party would not have the advantage
it has among white voters.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:30.860
And this is why you might see American politics
and you say there's more support for abortion

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:35.329
today than there has been at any time since
Roe v. Wade.

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:41.909
And yet, they say the Republicans still kowtow
to being against abortion and they still try

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:42.909
to play.

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:46.090
You know, they trump speaking at the March
for Life and all of this different stuff.

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:52.700
The reason why is that they are dependent
on the white evangelical voter, not only for

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.729
votes, but also for donations.

00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:58.649
Evangelicals are just over a third of white
voters.

00:01:58.649 --> 00:02:01.210
OK, so you've got all white voters.

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:03.630
A third of white voters are evangelical.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:04.689
They voted for Trump.

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:12.030
Roughly four to one, 80 to 20 other white
voters went for Hillary, 56 to 44, according

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.800
to exit polls against Trump in 2016.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:21.110
So when you slice and dice the electorate,
you start to understand that the analysis

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:26.640
that white people prefer Republicans, it's
not really getting at the core of the issue,

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.270
which in this particular case is religiosity.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:36.020
Now, anytime you look at these distinctions,
you have to be able to separate causation

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:37.380
vs. correlation.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:43.500
OK, I don't know exactly how that affects
the white voter element of it.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:51.610
But for example, with education, you see that
people without a college degree are the most

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:54.430
likely educationally to be voting for Trump.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:58.900
People with a college degree support Joe Biden
by by a pretty big margin.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.810
People with a post graduate degree support
Joe Biden by an even higher margin.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:06.720
The more education you have, the more likely
you are to support Biden over Trump.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.530
I actually believe that is causal.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:15.250
I think that education as a process makes
you less likely to be bamboozled by stupid

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.980
talking points from Trump.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.600
Like I know all about trade and I will fix
it.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.130
The more educated you are, the more likely
you are to realize Trump knows nothing about

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.650
trade and he's not going to fix it and you
shouldn't fall for it.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:33.730
So that is causal to me with some of these
other things religion, race, whatever.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:38.880
I think that we have to explore whether the
correlations have a causal component.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.560
That's sort of not really what we were taking
head on, but that's the situation.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:49.160
Yes, white voters support Republicans, but
were it not for white evangelicals, that support

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.090
would be very much in question.

